WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.672
Click + at the bottom left → Create Part Studio.

00:00:07.222 --> 00:00:11.762
Right-click the tab → Rename → Wheel and Bearing.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:16.352
Sketch on the Top plane. Press N.

00:00:16.902 --> 00:00:25.911
Line from the origin to the right. Press Q: construction. It's the axle line.

00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:33.822
Two center-point rectangles above the line: wide (tire) on top, narrow (hub) below.

00:00:34.372 --> 00:00:41.814
Top rectangle: 36 mm wide. Type mm after the number.

00:00:42.364 --> 00:00:52.070
Bottom rectangle: 0.5 in wide. Top line + centerline, drag below the centerline → a diameter.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.219
Ø54 mm: the outside of the wheel.

00:00:56.769 --> 00:01:11.188
Middle line: Ø22 mm. Hole: Ø0.25 in. If it flips below the line, dimension from the middle line instead.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:20.678
Revolve: both rectangles, axis = construction line, Full.

00:01:21.228 --> 00:01:25.919
Rename the part Wheel. P hides the planes.

00:01:26.469 --> 00:01:30.149
Fillet the outer edges.

00:01:30.699 --> 00:01:33.323
Now it looks like a real wheel.

00:01:33.873 --> 00:01:39.469
Side view. The flat ring around the hole is where the bearing sits.

00:01:40.019 --> 00:01:43.920
Extrude that face: New, 7 mm.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.037
Rename it Bearing.

00:01:46.587 --> 00:01:54.552
Sketch on the bearing face: two circles on the center.

00:01:55.102 --> 00:02:01.673
1 mm in from each edge: Ø20 mm and Ø8.35 mm.

00:02:02.223 --> 00:02:08.515
Ring: Remove, 0.5 mm. That's the bearing groove.

00:02:09.065 --> 00:02:15.254
Materials: Bearing = Stainless Steel 316. Wheel = Polyurethane.

00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:18.648
Edit appearance: pick a wheel color.

00:02:19.198 --> 00:02:25.932
Mass properties: ≈ 0.23 lb for one wheel and bearing.

00:02:26.482 --> 00:02:31.126
One wheel and bearing. Lesson 2.4 puts four on the board.
